/target
target/
/crates/*/gen
node_modules
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
*.log
# Except the TeX logs proton-tex's tests `include_str!`. They are fixtures, not
# output, and without them a fresh checkout's proton-tex does not compile.
!crates/proton-tex/tests/fixtures/*.log
.venv/

# Conversations. A user's project commits these if they want them — they are
# Chat mode's document and they diff like any other. Ignored *here* because
# `crates/proton-core/tests/agent.rs` roots a workspace at this repo on
# purpose, so that the agent's grep runs against the real index, and every
# question those tests ask now writes a file.
.proton/chats/
# One developer's theme and provider are not the project's. The file is
# designed to be committable — a team that wants the same editor can — but
# that is a decision somebody makes, not something `git add -A` does.
.proton/settings.json
# Same again, and swept in by exactly the `git add -A` that line warns about.
# It registers this checkout's `proton-mcp.exe` with the Codex CLI by absolute
# path, so it is true on one machine and wrong on every other.
.codex/
